%========================================================================
% MB-THEME-COVER — FRONT AND BACK COVER
%========================================================================
%
% Front cover:
%   Full-bleed navy background, crimson wedge, gold orbit, damped
%   oscillation and logarithmic growth curves, a semi-transparent
%   IDE-style C++ code specimen, compact equations, and direction
%   arrows. The design is unchanged from v1.1.
%
% Back cover (redesigned):
%   Static two-block layout:
%     - Ivory background (coverpaper).
%     - A single thin crimson rule at the top (visual anchor).
%     - Two static blocks separated by exactly 0.7cm:
%         1. "درباره این کتاب" — larger, primary block.
%         2. "درباره این نویسنده" — smaller, secondary block.
%     - A footer with MatinBook, the repository URL, and the
%       source link.
%     - All content is placed inside a fixed-height minipage
%       (\dimexpr\paperheight-8.9cm\relax), so no amount of text
%       can overflow onto a second page.
%
% RTL note (important):
%   A `minipage` does NOT inherit the surrounding RTL direction.
%   Without an explicit RTL group, the content of the back cover
%   renders left-to-right, which is wrong for Persian.
%
%   To fix this, the back cover body is wrapped in a `\beginR ...
%   \endR` group (from xepersian/bidi). This forces the minipage
%   contents to be laid out right-to-left.
%
%   Additionally, we use `\raggedright` instead of `\raggedleft`.
%   In an RTL context, `\raggedright` means "flush to the right
%   edge of the line", which is the desired alignment for Persian.
%
% Author bio API:
%   \authorbio{متن درباره نویسنده}
%     Optional. If set, the "About the Author" block is rendered.
%     If not set, the block is omitted and only the "About This
%     Book" block is shown.
%
%   This preserves backward compatibility with the previous
%   \makebackcover{blurb} API.
%
%========================================================================


